    "image_with_text_TEjFMB": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_zdD9k9": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Tianna McFarlane",
            "heading_size": "ts-text-clamp_l"
          }
        },
        "text_YzYBYF": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>is a pioneering entrepreneur and the visionary founder of Heal In Colour, a groundbreaking Canadian company that creates adhesive bandages specifically designed for black and brown skin tones. Through this innovative venture, she has not only transformed the bandage industry but also championed greater representation of diverse skin tones in everyday products.<\/p><p>With a diploma in Business Operations Management from Durham College, Tianna's entrepreneurial journey has been driven by a deep commitment to effecting positive change. Her mission is clear: to make bandages for black and brown skin tones the norm, not the exception, challenging and reshaping societal norms along the way.<\/p><p>Tianna's work has garnered significant recognition, including being named a Changemaker by the Toronto Star, an acknowledgment of her dedication to inclusivity, innovation, and empowerment. Her influence extends beyond revolutionizing the bandage market; she is also passionate about inspiring and uplifting Black women entrepreneurs, serving as a powerful role model for those striving to carve out their own paths in the business world.<\/p><p>Tianna McFarlane embodies the spirit of a true changemaker, leaving a lasting impact on her industry and paving the way for a future where diversity and representation are not just goals but fundamental elements of everyday life.<\/p>",
            "text_style": "body",
            "use_color": false,
            "text_color": "#000000"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_zdD9k9",
        "text_YzYBYF"
      ],
      "custom_css": [
        ".global-media-settings {border: 0;}",
        ".image-with-text__text.rte {max-width: 90rem;}",
        "@media only screen and (min-width: 750px) {.gradient > div {padding: 0 !important; } .image-with-text__content {padding-top: 7vw; padding-bottom: 7vw; }}",
